<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!-- Haven round 6, launcher icon ONLY (worker C).
         DARK-RENDER FINDING (verified from the actual round-5
         resources, not assumed): the device path breaks the
         BACKGROUND layer — the round-5 comments record that
         Garrett's Fold8 recents pane blackened the solid lime
         #9BF67C field (One UI forced dark icons / Android
         auto-theming) while the foreground rendered intact. The
         round-5 fix (bright off-white tile + charcoal house) kept
         the launcher grid legible, but it did not cure the
         unfolded recents task pane — the acceptance case — because
         the construction still depended on a light field carrying
         a near-black (#161D17) mark: blacken the field and the
         dark mark vanishes into it. This redesign removes that
         failure mode entirely: there is no tile/plate and no dark
         mark anywhere. The field is a deep green and the mark is
         WHITE line art, so even if a device path blackens the
         field outright, white-on-black still reads (21:1).
         FIELD: full-bleed Haven leaf green #3E6B2F — the light
         theme primary in Theme.kt, and the round-5 spark color.
         CONTRAST (WCAG relative luminance): white on #3E6B2F =
         6.27:1, passing AA for normal text. White on pale lime
         #9BF67C is 1.32:1 and was rejected for exactly that
         reason. #1B3708 forest (13.15:1) was rejected because at
         icon sizes it reads as near-black, defeating the green
         identity; #3E6B2F is the deepest green that still reads
         unambiguously green.
         MARK: white line-art house, same geometry family as the
         round-5 mark (pitched roof, body, door opening), drawn as
         strokes (4.5dp, round caps/joins) — not a filled
         silhouette, not a tile. The filled leaf spark is dropped:
         a filled accent does not translate to stroke at 48dp and
         the roof/body/door alone carry the Haven house.
         SAFE ZONE (center 54,54, radius 33): roof corners
         (30,52)/(78,52) sit ~24.1dp out, apex (54,30) 24dp out,
         body corners (36,76)/(72,76) ~28.4dp out; with a 2.25dp
         half-stroke the outermost ink stays under ~30.7dp, so
         circle, squircle, square, rectangle, and expressive
         masks (including Samsung's default shape) never clip
         critical content. Roof overhangs the body eaves line by
         6dp per side, as a real roofline should. -->
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="4.5"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M30,52 L54,30 L78,52" />
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="4.5"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M36,52 H72 V76 H36 Z" />
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="4.5"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M48,76 V64 Q48,62 50,62 H58 Q60,62 60,64 V76" />
</vector>
